  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122428,
      "SummaryText": "General Executive Summary for Chemical, Manufacturing and Oil Refining Facilities\n\n1. Accidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies\nWe at Brenntag Mid-South, Inc. are strongly committed to employee, public and environmental safety. This commitment is inherent to a comprehensive accidental release prevention program in place that covers areas such as design, installation, operating procedures, maintenance, and employee training associated with the processes at our facility. It is our policy to implement\nappropriate controls to prevent possible releases of regulated substances. Unforeseeably, if such a release does occur, we are coordinated with REIDSVILLE FIRE DEPARTMENT which provides trained emergency response personnel to control and mitigate the effects of the release.  \n\n2. The Stationary Source and the Regulated Substances Handled Our facility's primary activities encompass Storage and Distribution of chemical products. We have 3 regulated substances present at our facility. These substances include Chlorine, Aqua Ammonia (Ammonium Hydroxide Solution) and Sulfur Dioxide. All three (3) products are received prepackaged in containers, warehoused and resold to our customers. \n\n3. The General Accidental Release Prevention Program and the Chemical-Specific Prevention Steps Our facility has taken all the necessary steps to comply with the accidental release prevention requirements set out under 40 CFR part 68 of the EPA. The following sections briefly describe the elements of our release prevention program that are in place at our stationary source. \n\nProcess Safety Information\n\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. maintains written safety information that describes the chemical hazards, and equipment designs associated storing and distributing the covered chemicals.  \n\nOperating Procedures\n\nFor the purposes of safely conducting activities within our covered processes, Brenntag Mid-South, Inc. maintains written operating procedures. The information is regularly r"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000122428,
      "SummaryText": "eviewed and is readily accessible to operators involved with the processes.\n\nTraining\n\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. has a comprehensive training program in place to ensure that employees are competent in the applicable handling and operating procedures.\n\nMechanical Integrity\n\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. carries out documented maintenance checks on material handling equipment to ensure proper functions.  Maintenance operations are carried out by qualified personnel with previous training in maintenance practices. Furthermore, these personnel are offered specialized training as needed. Any equipment deficiencies identified by the maintenance checks are corrected in a safe and timely\nmanner.\n\nManagement of Change\nWritten procedures are in place at Brenntag Mid-South, Inc. to manage changes in process chemicals,technology, equipment and procedures. \n\nCompliance Audits\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. conducts audits on a regular basis to determine whether the provisions set out under the RMP rule are being implemented. These audits are carried out at least every 3 years. \n\nIncident Investigation\nBrenntag, Inc. promptly investigates any incident that has resulted in, or could reasonably result in a catastrophic release of a regulated substance. These investigations are undertaken to identify the situation leading to the incident as well as any corrective actions to prevent the release from reoccurring. All reports are retained for a minimum of 5 years.\n\nEmployee Participation\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. involves employees as applicable and strongly encourages them to express their views concerning accident prevention issues and to recommend improvements. I\n\nContractors\nOn occasion, our company hires contractors to conduct specialized maintenance and construction activities. Prior to selecting a contractor, a thorough evaluation of safety performance of the contractor is carried out. Brenntag Mid-South, Inc. has a strict policy of informing the contractors of known potential hazards relate"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 2,
      "FacilityID": 1000122428,
      "SummaryText": "d to the contractors work and the processes. Contractors are also informed of all the procedures for emergency response should an accidental release of a regulated substance occur.\n\n4. Five-year Accident History\n\nBrenntag Mid-South, INC. Duncan, SC facility has had 0 accidental releases over the last 5\nyears.\n\n5. Emergency Response Plan\n\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. carries a written emergency response plan to deal with accidental releases of hazardous materials. The emergency response plan is a comprehensive plan outlining different emergency conditions, notification of local emergency response agencies and the public. To ensure proper functioning, our emergency response equipment is regularly inspected and serviced. In addition, the plan is promptly updated to reflect any pertinent changes taking place within our processes that would require a modified emergency response. REIDSVILLE FIRE DEPARTMENT is the agency with which our emergency plan has been coordinated and verified.\n\n6. Planned Changes to Improve Safety\nBrenntag Mid-South, Inc. constantly strives to improve the safety of the processes at the Duncan facility through the incident investigation program, safety committee, near miss reporting, hazard analysis and auditing programs. At the time of this resubmission there were no planned changes to improve safety."
    }
  ]
